    <item>
      <title>security-guidance: use the CA file macOS ships when Python has none</title>
      <link>https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/commit/7d95efc2dce00c0eae8307aaa261f6c65e8e6236</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">7d95efc</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:54:17 GMT</pubDate>
      <category>gh-commits-plugins-official</category>
      <description>A python.org Python on macOS has no CA certificates until its &quot;Install Certificates&quot; command is run, so every review from it failed to verify the API&apos;s certificate. Where Python&apos;s default TLS context holds no certificate at all, the plugin now adds /etc/ssl/cert.pem, the file Apple&apos;s own Python uses</description>
    </item>
